B1:mult-positivity.first_theorem:
THEOREM (Mollified inertia certificate, Regime I). Fix lambda in (1/2, 1), theta in [0, (1-lambda)/2], delta > 0 with lambda + 2*theta <= 1 - delta. Let L = lambda*log(T/2pi), M = (T/2pi)^theta, and let phi, f_k, d be exactly as in the two-thirds paper. Let b_m = mu(m)*psi(log(M/m)/log M) for a fixed C^2 profile psi >= 0, psi(0)=0 — or, in the general form, any real b with b_1 = 1, |b_m| <= 1, supp b in [1,M] — normalized by n(b) = sum b_m^2/m. Define G^B_kl = W(b*f_k, b*f_l) (multiplicative convolution). Then, unconditionally:
(i) [Structure] G^B/(aL^2) = P_B + Q_B + E_B with P_B PSD, rank P_B <= s1+s2, n_+(Q_B) <= p, and ||E_B|| <= C(phi) l^3 T^{(lambda+2theta)/2 - 1};
(ii) [Moments] tr G^B/(aL^2) = (m1(b,lambda) + O(E_T)) N(T,2T) and ||G^B/(aL^2)||_F^2 = (m2(b,lambda) + O(E_T)) N(T,2T), where m1 = n(b) + 2*C(b)-correlation term and m2 = [window-Plancherel <|B|^4>-term/lambda_1] + [mollified prime diagonal] + [mollifier-prime cross-diagonal with triangle weight] — each an explicit finite multiplicative sum, with all off-diagonal contributions << L^2 * X M^2 * (log)^2 via Montgomery-Vaughan (Lemma 5.2 verbatim), and E_T the paper's error budget with X -> XM^2;
(iii) [Certificate] N_0^dist(T,2T) >= (2*m1(b,lambda)^2/m2(b,lambda) - 1 - o(1)) N(T,2T), via n_+(H) >= (tr H)_+^2/||H||_F^2, inertia pull-back, and N >= N_on + 2p;
(iv) [First variation] d/d(eps)[m1^2/m2] at b = delta_1 in the direction of the normalized Moebius profile equals sum_p (log p/p) G(alpha_p) psi-weights + o(1), with G an explicit elementary function of alpha = log p/log(T/2pi) determined by phi (flat window weight on the trace gain vs Fejer triangle weight on the cross-diagonal cost).
STATUS OF INPUTS: (i) is the paper's Prop 4.1/4.2 with two new 20-line lemmas (signature of [[0,w],[conj w,0]] for complex w; tail with the M-factor) — inputs fully proven. (iii) is Lemma 3.3 + Lemma 3.1 + RvM — all in the Lean repo already. (ii) is the genuinely new analytic work: mollified first moment via Landau-Gonek (unconditional; uniformity in M <= T^theta to be checked against Gonek's explicit version — flagged), mollified second moment by the paper's own reduction (Lemma 5.4-5.7) with b-weighted coefficients, off-diagonals killed by MV exactly as in Prop 5.6 since total length XM^2 <= T^{1-delta}. Standard Levinson-grade bookkeeping, no new conjectural input. (iv) is a finite computation once (ii)'s main terms are written. ATTACK: write (ii) as the paper does — six bilinear pieces of nu_B x nu_B against L^2 Phi^2 — with the one new main term (mollifier-prime cross-diagonal at matched frequency log p, which the unmollified paper's oscillation argument killed); assemble (iii); evaluate G numerically and in closed form; publish with the sign verdict for short Moebius vs short resonator directions. The theorem is referee-evaluable, its unmollified specialization (b = delta_1) reproduces the paper's 1/2-distinct branch as a consistency check, and it is non-restating: no famous conjecture appears as hypothesis or conclusion.

B2:refutation-program.first_theorem:
THEOREM (Localized certificate; the wanted poster). For every θ ∈ (3−√6, 1] and ε > 0 there exists T₀(θ,ε) such that for all T ≥ T₀ and every H with T^θ ≤ H ≤ T, writing I = (T, T+H], N(I) for nontrivial zeros with ordinate in I counted with multiplicity, N₀ˢ(I) for simple zeros on Re s = 1/2, N_d(I) for distinct zeros, and N_off(I) for zeros with Re ρ ≠ 1/2 counted with multiplicity:
(a) N₀ˢ(I) ≥ (2 − 1/θ − θ/3 − ε)·N(I);
(b) N_off(I) ≤ (1/θ + θ/3 − 1 + ε)·N(I);
(c) N_d(I) ≥ ((3 − 1/θ − θ/3)/2 − ε)·N(I);
uniformly over the window position T, and — the point — uniformly over the depths |β−1/2| ∈ (0,1/2) of whatever off-line zeros exist. Refinement: with the Montgomery–Taylor window, 1/θ + θ/3 improves to 1/c*_θ, c*_θ = √2·tan(θ/√2)/(1+(θ/√2)tan(θ/√2)).
COROLLARY (anti-clustering, depth-uniform): there is no height γ₀ and window of length ≥ γ₀^{0.5506} in which more than a fraction (1/θ+θ/3−1+ε) of zeros are off the critical line; in particular a hypothetical counterexample's off-line companions have local density ≤ 1/3+ε at scale γ₀ and its γ₀^θ-neighborhoods carry a certified majority of simple on-line zeros.
STATUS OF INPUTS: every input is proven and formalized — EF for C_c² test functions (WeilEF/), grid-translation-invariant Gabor–Poisson (Poisson.lean), block structure and inertia for arbitrary windows (ZeroBlockData, ZeroSide.lean), rank–trace (RankTrace.lean), MV with the window-independent off-diagonal bound (PPOffDiag.lean), short-interval Riemann–von Mangoldt from the local count N(t+1)−N(t) ≤ A₀log(t+3) already in PaperInputs. The ONLY new work is re-running the prime-side moment evaluation (Props 5.5–5.7) with window length H as a parameter: main terms localize because μ is flat across I and the diagonal prime term scales linearly in H; the binding check is O₁ ≪ L²X = o(HL³) ⟺ λ < θ, and the tail/boundary bookkeeping with D₀ = T^{θ/4+ε} (allowed by Prop 4.2's stated D₀-range), N(I′∖I) ≪ D₀·l = o(Hl). ATTACK SKETCH: (1) restate the Facts structures of PrimeSideB with (T,2T] → (T,T+H]; (2) verify each of the six bilinear pieces of Lemma 5.4/Props 5.5–5.7 carries an H-linear main term and window-free error (the dangerous ones are the cross terms 𝓜[μ,P_X] ≪ l√X and ends E1/E2 — check no integration-by-parts boundary term proportional to T rather than H survives; if one does, replace the sharp window by a C³-in-position weight, costing o(1)); (3) feed count_certificate (already parametric in κ and N) and take λ → θ⁻. A referee can evaluate every step against the published Prop 5.5–5.7 proofs.
